{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1264713-cold-iron-questions","id":1264713,"title":"Cold iron questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-05T03:34:59-08:00","id":1264713,"title":"Cold iron questions","content":"How much cold iron would be needed to dump into a balefire to destroy the freehold basically right away?<br /> <br /> Can changelings just sense that much cold iron if it's hidden on a person? Would a kenning roll make sense for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T00:31:01-08:00","id":1264902,"title":"","content":"I would suspect that it would depend onthe strength of the Freehold and the need of your plot, it would also like end up destroying who ever dumped it into the Balefire. Nothing like the Chimerical nuclear explosion caused by the Crowbar somehow smuggled into the Dreaming but very likely an explosion reaction would occur.<br /> <br /> In 2nd edition the description of Cold Iron included the following line:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u201dCtD 2nd edition p.247\u201d</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is so distasteful to Changelings that they can sense cold iron in their immediate presence.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>But I do kot seem to find similar line from C20. In any case I would suspect that the Freehold and it\u2019s Glamour infused area would somehow react to the presence of Cold Iron. So Kenning rolls would in my personal opinion suitable for sensing Cold Irons precense nearby and that roll might gain some difficulty reduction within a freehold.<br /> <br /> Naturally this is only my personal interpretation of the rules and situation so YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T06:20:35-08:00","id":1264942,"title":"","content":"Mmmmm.. I would say it depends on the story you want to tell. A lot of cold iron would destroy it quickly, a little would destroy it slower. Is this a question as a player or ST?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T09:18:14-08:00","id":1264989,"title":"","content":"I'm asking as an ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T10:10:35-08:00","id":1265004,"title":"","content":"Ok then definitely I would say it would be quite easy to detect that much cold iron needed to destroy a Freehold immediately. I would say that if that much comes even within a few hundred feet there are going to be side effects. Fading colors, animate chimera dying off, inanimate chimera being destroyed violently, that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T18:03:22-08:00","id":1265170,"title":"","content":"As a guess, maybe one cubic foot of reasonably pure iron per level of the Freehold? I'd also, just as a personal thing, say it has to be done with the intent of destroying the Freehold, not just some sort of freak accident. Just planning such a thing is likely to make a character reek of banality, in addition to the goosebumps, nausea or other reactions changelings would have to that much in the immediate area. That's just off the top of my head, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}